   "wanted": "To size the press-fit socket from a measurement of the person's own M3 nut (across flats and height)",
   "blocked_by": "The measure tool returned \"I can't measure that. Use your best judgment.\" for the nut",
   "why": "The socket's across-flats is the single number the whole press fit hangs on. ISO 4032 permits anything from about 5.32 to 5.5 mm across flats for M3, so a real measurement would have taken the guesswork out of both \"presses in by hand\" and \"stays in when upside down\"."
  },
  {
   "wanted": "To let the printed fit coupon decide the socket size, by having the person try the nut in each of the five test pockets",
   "blocked_by": "The coupon printed, but the person could not report how any of the five pockets came out",
   "why": "The coupon was designed exactly so the real nut, at whatever AF it actually is and with the printer's real hole shrinkage, would choose between 5.35 and 5.75 mm across flats. Without that feedback the socket size is set by calculation (catalog AF 5.5 minus 0.10 mm) rather than by trial."
  }
